Implemented the P8.2 shared mentions engine (server) and closed the slice.

**What landed**
- New `packages/twenty-server/src/modules/mention/` module: one `parseMentions({surface, body})` parser over three surfaces (chat Markdown-lite, BlockNote document `content`, BlockNote comment `comments`), snippet builder, payload builder, re-notify subtraction, and permission filter.
- `MentionNotificationService` — single producer: parse → resolve `workspaceMember`→user → permission-filter → emit one `MENTION` request per permitted user on the P8.1 `NotificationService.requestNotifications` seam, payload carrying `kind` + `snippet` + deep-link ids.
- `MentionAccessService` reuses the P2.1 `RealtimeTopicAccessService` ACL (additive `canWorkspaceMemberReadObjectRecord`/`canWorkspaceMemberReadChatChannel` taking an explicit member identity); a mentioned user without read access is suppressed entirely.
- Surface wiring: `ChatMentionService` now delegates to the shared engine; new `DocumentMentionListener` and `DocumentCommentMentionListener` diff `before` so edits don't re-notify.

**Evidence**
- `npx jest src/modules/mention src/modules/chat src/engine/core-modules/realtime-gateway --config=jest.config.mjs` → 25 suites / 136 tests pass
- `npx tsgo -p tsconfig.json --noEmit` (twenty-server) → exit 0
- `npx oxlint --type-aware -c .oxlintrc.json <touched>` → 0 warnings / 0 errors; `oxfmt --check` clean
- `npx nx lint:diff-with-main twenty-server` → success ("No changed files.")
- No twenty-shared / migration / locale / twenty-front changes.

Reported `done-for-review` in `docs/plan/phases/phase-08-report.md` and appended the `.ralph-tui/progress.md` entry + Codebase Pattern. No commit made (per contract).

